BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus by Emma Knight - By the Lake 
 Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T190000
UID:344a975fb859ef9c06c802fc17fd9e71@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus\, by Emma Knight\, shortl
 isted for the 2025 Scotiabank Giller Prize\, is a spellbinding debut about
  friendship\, motherhood\, first love and the secrets that shape us. Set a
 gainst the moody backdrop of Edinburgh\, the novel follows Pen\, a Canadia
 n student unraveling a family mystery while navigating independence and de
 sire. With wit and emotional depth\, Knight explores womanhood and the cho
 ices that bind us. By the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events fr
 om February to December with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics 
 alumni. Each in-person event features readings\, discussions\, Q&A\, book 
 signings and ASL interpretation\, while virtual sessions include live subt
 itles and audio access.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicoke\, ON
URL:https://secure.toronto.ca/webapps/feps_edc-ticketing/#events/4c24b080-
 834a-499a-8d4f-4dd578c9d279
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T100000
UID:824d515a402d872a52f7458631624467@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to chall
 enge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynam
 ics\, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each pie
 ce is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by
  Danielle Colle. About the Artist Danielle Cole is a Toronto-based artist 
 whose collages\, composed of vintage graphics\, examine domestic roles and
  consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and featured in 
 CBC Arts\, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall Gallery\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicok
 e\, ON
URL:daniellecole.ca
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
